WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
Speaker 1: Congresswoman Nancy Pelosi will no&nbsp;
longer be in leadership. She is currently the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.100
speaker of the House. That speakership is set to&nbsp;
end when Republicans take control of the House in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.020
January of 2023. And Nancy Pelosi announced&nbsp;
on the floor of the House yesterday she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:21.720
not going to be seeking a leadership role, but&nbsp;
she will be staying in Congress. The Associated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:28.260
Press reporting that this is a, quote, pivotal&nbsp;
realignment making way for a new generation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:34.260
leaders. Nancy Pelosi gave a speech. She said&nbsp;
that, first of all, she has led Democrats for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:40.500
nearly 20 years. Secondly, she is dealing with the&nbsp;
aftermath of this brutal attack on her husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:47.160
Paul Pelosi, last month in their San Francisco&nbsp;
home. She was the first female speaker of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:53.700
House and she will not seek any leadership role&nbsp;
starting in January. She says We must move boldly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.500
into the future. I will not seek reelection&nbsp;
to Democratic leadership in the next Congress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:05.880
for me. The hour has come for a new generation&nbsp;
to lead the Democratic caucus that I so deeply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:13.620
respect. She received a standing ovation and&nbsp;
it is not typical that a party leader stays on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:21.120
after withdrawing from the leadership. She was&nbsp;
reelected and there is much speculation about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:27.660
whether this will be her final two year term.&nbsp;
She is 82 years old. We don't know the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:35.100
to that. But Nancy Pelosi made it clear and it is&nbsp;
horrifying when you are influenced in your plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.640
by such a horrifying attack, like what happened&nbsp;
to Paul Pelosi, because to some degree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:47.820
you feel as though you're I'm letting them push&nbsp;
me out. But there were already questions about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:54.120
Nancy Pelosi's future. Whatever you think about&nbsp;
her politics and I am to Nancy Pelosi's left,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:01.440
you have to recognize not only the significance&nbsp;
as the first female speaker of the House,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:09.780
but her 20 year tenure in Democratic leadership&nbsp;
and her ability to get things done there. Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.020
necessarily the most exciting things, always.&nbsp;
They're not necessarily the things I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:18.540
prioritize. But she did understand how the&nbsp;
House of Representatives worked. And while I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:25.140
have taken issue with Nancy Pelosi so many times&nbsp;
on specifics, quite a career. Quite a career. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:30.180
Nancy Pelosi, stepping down from leadership,&nbsp;
will stay in the House of Representatives

